# Python (12x12) color=0xF4
# The two interlocking snakes of the Python logo, in the logo's yellow
# (#FFD43B -> RGB332 0xF4). Each snake keeps its eye as a hole: upper left
# for the top snake, lower right for the bottom one. The tails are what
# makes the mark readable this small, so they get a third of the height
# each and overlap only in the middle two rows: the left half is filled
# rows 3-6 and the right half rows 5-8, which is the step the real mark
# has where the two bodies cross.
....111.....
...11111....
...1.111....
.1111111....
1111111.....
11111..1111.
.111.1111111
....11111111
....1111111.
....111.1...
....11111...
.....111....
